    "note": "Field uniform (Feldanzug, Heer): the olive rank slide (Aufschiebeschlaufe) on the camouflage shoulder strap, devices woven in black (BPrDGrUnifAnO para 5(3): black or white replace silver on the Kampfanzug; TL 8455-0009 Anhang A 'DG Schwarz auf Oliv'). Medium (official-text extracts): device kinds and counts per Anlage 2 (1-4 Schraegstreifen; Tresse open at the bottom / closed; closed Tresse with 1 or 2 Winkel point up or a Kopfwinkel; 1 or 2 stars); the Litze in the Waffenfarbe on the Feldanzug strap, Heer only, 4 mm wide (bundeswehr.de), green (Jaegergruen) for Panzergrenadiere. Medium-low: slide 90 mm long, 52 mm wide at the collar end, 60 mm at the shoulder end (one TL 8455-0009 extract and a shop; not reproduced). Low (inferred, no drawing readable): every device size and the exact millimetres (stripes 5 mm with 3 mm gaps at 35 deg, the lowest 5 mm above the shoulder end, the Stabsgefreiter's fourth 9 mm above the third; Tresse 7 mm, 2 mm in; Winkel 5 mm band, 100 deg, the lowest one's legs ending 4 mm above the Tresse at the shoulder end, the next 10 mm higher; stars four-pointed faceted pips, 17 mm, inner radius 0.42, the first centred 20 mm above the shoulder end, the next 20 mm higher). Owner (2026-11-15, binding): every device is built up from the shoulder end (Gefreiter stripe and Leutnant star at the bottom; the Stabsgefreiter's top stripe set apart from the three below), the Kopfwinkel's shape (drawn Odal-like: a 5 mm band, legs crossing under an 11 mm diamond head), the stripes' direction, the strap's shape (as wide as the slide, following its taper) and colour, the Litze's place 3 mm below the slide and its hex colour. Search extracts only; no page could be opened."
  },
